  accounts/         # User+Team+Membership
{%- if use_attachments %}
  attachments/      # file uploads
{%- endif %}
{%- if use_notifications %}
  notifications/    # in-app notifications
{%- endif %}
  example/          # placeholder; delete when you add your domain
config/           # Django project config (settings, urls, wsgi, asgi)
templates/        # project-level templates
static/           # project-level static files
compose/          # Docker build context
```

## Testing

```bash
uv run pytest
uv run ruff check .
uv run ruff format --check .
uv run python manage.py check
{%- if use_drf %}
uv run python manage.py spectacular --validate --fail-on-warn
{%- endif %}
```

## Deploy

```bash
docker compose -f compose.yaml -f compose.production.yml up -d
```

CI runs the same checks via `.gitlab-ci.yml`. The `deploy-check` job validates `manage.py check --deploy` against the fail-fast guards in `config/settings/production.py`.

